# Third-party notices and attribution

Ravan-AI trains small language models from random initialization on the
following third-party material. This file must accompany distributions of the
corpus files and, as good practice, of derived model weights.

## Persian Wikipedia (2018 dump)

- Content: articles from the Persian edition of Wikipedia.
- Licence: **CC BY-SA 4.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)
- Attribution: © Persian Wikipedia contributors, https://fa.wikipedia.org
- Packaging used for acquisition: github.com/Text-Mining/Persian-Wikipedia-Corpus
- ShareAlike notice: modified redistributions of the corpus text must remain
  under CC BY-SA 4.0 with attribution.

## MIZAN parallel corpus

- Content: Persian–English sentence-aligned literary translations.
- Licence: **CC BY 4.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
- Attribution: Omid Kashefi, "MIZAN: a large persian-english parallel corpus"
  (2018), https://github.com/omidkashefi/Mizan, arXiv:1801.02107

## Ganjoor classical poetry

- Content: verses of classical Persian poets (Ferdowsi, Saadi, Hafez,
  Khayyam, Attar, Jami, Saeb, Khajoo, Bahar, Asadi, Anvari) as digitized by
  Ganjoor (https://ganjoor.net).
- Status: public-domain literary works; only verse text was used. AI-generated
  summaries and biographies on the site were deliberately excluded.

## Project-authored material

- `data/raw/pretrain.txt`, `data/raw/instructions*.jsonl`,
  `data/raw/instructions_v2_part*.jsonl` and all repository code/docs are
  original to this repository (currently published without an OSI licence —
  see the repository landing page).

## Disclaimer

Model outputs are statistical patterns learned from the material above; they
are **not verifiable facts** and may be confidently wrong. The model has no
internet access and no retrieval system.
